      "title": "Trump admits Iran war led to poll loss, but says would 'do it again'",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/trump-admits-iran-war-led-to-poll-loss-but-says-would-do-it-again-126110500038_1.html",
      "description": "US President Donald Trump on Wednesday said it was \"largely true\" that the war in Iran cost the Republicans heavy losses in the midterm election, but struck a defiant note, saying he would do it again as it was the \"only answer\" in the \"long term\".\n\"Well, I think it's largely true because it drove the gasoline up a little bit short term,\" Trump told reporters when asked about Vice President J D Vance's remarks that the Iran war led to Republican losses in the election.\n\"But at the same time, if I had it to do again, I'd have to do it again. Because long term, it's the only answer. You can't let Iran have a nuclear weapon,\" he said.\nThe president insisted that the US would have done nothing different as far as the war was concerned.\n\"But I can tell you that as far as that war is concerned, I would have done nothing different. We've totally broken their military. The navy's gone. Their air force is gone. Their anti-aircraft is gone,\" Trump said.\n\"The Iran thing, we had to do, and we",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-05T02:38:02"
