    {
      "title": "Vance tries to distance himself from Iran war after GOP loses in midterms",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/vance-tries-to-distance-himself-from-iran-war-after-gop-loses-in-midterms-126110500032_1.html",
      "description": "JD Vance publicly broke from President Donald Trump's defence of the Iran war Wednesday after the Republican Party's deep losses in the midterm elections, attempting to distance himself from voters' clear rebuke of the president as the vice president faces questions about his own political ambitions.\nVance, who has said he would decide after the election whether to run for president in 2028, issued a lengthy social media post blaming the unpopular conflict with Iran for the GOP's drubbing.\nVance said, \"If you'd like to argue it was worth it, that losing the Senate for the next 6 years was worth it, then do so.\"\nBut arguing that the war was worth it is what Trump repeatedly did on the campaign trail, continued to do in interviews as election results came in and did again Wednesday morning.\nAs he led reporters on an impromptu visit to the ballroom he's constructing at the White House, Trump said, \"The Iran thing, we had to do and we continue to do it.\"\nTrump said he spoke to Vance o",
